{"step_index":649,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T11:06:47Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-26T11:06:47Z\nCompleted At: 2026-10-26T11:06:48Z\nShowing lines 1-423 of 423\n1: ---\n2: name: kernel-fuse-diagnosis\n3: description: >\n4:   FUSE（用户态文件系统）内核端故障诊断技能。当用户提到 FUSE 文件系统 hang、\n5:   所有操作返回 EIO、FUSE daemon 崩溃/重启、请求队列阻塞、D 状态进程堆积、\n6:   /sys/fs/fuse/connections/ 异常、libfuse 兼容性、max_read/max_write 配置不当、\n7:   writeback cache 一致性问题、多线程 FUSE daemon 死锁、容器中 /dev/fuse 权限问题、\n8:   FUSE 性能退化等关键词时，必须使用本技能。\n9:   覆盖场景：FUSE daemon 崩溃后 EIO、请求队列阻塞与 D 状态、max_read/max_write 配置不当、\n10:   writeback cache 一致性问题、多线程 daemon 死锁、/dev/fuse 权限问题、内核 FUSE 模块 Bug、\n11:   混合复杂 FUSE 故障。即使只收到\"文件系统挂了\"、\"目录打不开\"、\"ls 卡死\"但挂载点\n12:   为 FUSE 类型时也应触发本技能。\n13:   支持 FUSE 全链路诊断（sysfs 队列 → 内核参数 → daemon 进程 → 代码级根因）。\n14: ---\n15: \n16: # FUSE 内核端故障诊断（三层下钻：系统层 → 类型层 → 代码根因层）\n17: \n18: ## 第一节：故障目录结构\n19: \n20: ```text\n21: fuse_case/                  # 故障案例目录\n22: ├── scripts/                # 【内置】本技能的诊断脚本\n23: │   ├── 01_baseline_info.sh\n24: │   ├── branch_A_daemon_crash.sh\n25: │   ├── branch_B_req_queue.sh\n26: │   ├── branch_C_max_read_write.sh\n27: │   ├── branch_D_writeback_cache.sh\n28: │   ├── branch_E_mt_deadlock.sh\n29: │   ├── branch_F_dev_fuse_perm.sh\n30: │   ├── branch_G_kernel_bug.sh\n31: │   └── branch_H_mixed.sh\n32: ├── logs/                   # 【可选】应用日志\n33: │   ├── application.log\n34: │   └── dmesg_output.txt\n35: ├── fuse_state/             # 【可选】故障时刻的 FUSE 状态快照\n36: │   ├── connections.txt     # ls /sys/fs/fuse/connections/\n37: │   ├── waiting.txt         # cat .../waiting\n38: │   └── abort.txt           # cat .../abort\n39: └── report/                 # 【输出】诊断报告目录\n40: ```\n41: \n42: ```bash\n43: # 检查 FUSE 文件系统挂载状态基线\n44: mount -t fuse\n45: ```\n46: \n47: ---\n48: \n49: ## 第二节：分析策略（三层下钻，逐层收敛）\n50: \n51: FUSE 内核端故障诊断采用**三层下钻模型**，从最外层逐层深入，层间存在依赖关系：\n52: \n53: ```\n54: ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n55: │                   三层下钻分析模型                                 │\n56: │                                                                 │\n57: │   L1: 系统层         mount -t fuse /proc/mounts                 │\n58: │       │               /sys/fs/fuse/connections/*                │\n59: │       └─ 判断：FUSE 挂载点是否正常？连接是否存在？               │\n60: │                                                                 │\n61: │   L2: 类型层         strace -p <daemon_pid>                     │\n62: │       │               cat /sys/fs/fuse/connections/*/waiting     │\n63: │       └─ 判断：是 EIO？请求阻塞？性能退化？权限问题？            │\n64: │                                                                 │\n65: │   L3: 代码/内核层    FUSE daemon 源码分析                       │\n66: │                      内核 FUSE 模块参数 (/sys/module/fuse/)     │\n67: │                      /dev/fuse 设备状态                          │\n68: │                      └─ 根因定位：daemon 崩溃 / 队列阻塞 / 配置  │\n69: │                                                                 │\n70: │   每层输出：证据 + 结论。L3 输出最终根因。                       │\n71: └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n72: ```\n73: \n74: ### 故障分类树\n75: \n76: ```\n77: L1 ─ FUSE 挂载点与连接检查\n78: │\n79: ├─ L2 ─ 挂载点正常？─────── 否 ──→ 非 FUSE 问题，转其他技能\n80: │                         是\n81: │                         ↓\n82: ├─ L2 ─ 操作返回 EIO？──── 是 ──→ Branch A (Daemon Crash)\n83: │                         否\n84: │                         ↓\n85: ├─ L2 ─ 进程 D 状态/Hang？ 是 ──→ Branch B (Req Queue) / Branch E (MT Deadlock)\n86: │                         否\n87: │                         ↓\n88: ├─ L2 ─ 性能退化？─────── 是 ──→ Branch C (Max Read/Write)\n89: │                         否\n90: │                         ↓\n91: ├─ L2 ─ 数据一致性异常？─ 是 ──→ Branch D (Writeback Cache)\n92: │                         否\n93: │                         ↓\n94: ├─ L2 ─ 权限问题？─────── 是 ──→ Branch F (dev/fuse Perm)\n95: │                         否\n96: │                         ↓\n97: ├─ L2 ─ 内核崩溃/Oops？── 是 ──→ Branch G (Kernel Bug)\n98: │                         否\n99: │                         ↓\n100: └─ L2 ─ 混合/复杂现象？── 是 ──→ Branch H (Mixed)\n101: ```\n102: \n103: ---\n104: \n105: ## 第三节：诊断流程\n106: \n107: ### L1: 系统层 — 基线采集与挂载点检查\n108: \n109: 检查系统 FUSE 基础配置与挂载状态，判断是否为系统级配置问题。\n110: \n111: ```bash\n112: # 1. 检查 FUSE 挂载点\n113: mount -t fuse\n114: \n115: # 2. 检查 /proc/mounts 中 FUSE 条目\n116: grep fuse /proc/mounts\n117: \n118: # 3. 检查 FUSE 内核连接状态\n119: ls /sys/fs/fuse/connections/ 2>/dev/null\n120: \n121: # 4. 检查 FUSE daemon 进程\n122: ps aux | grep -E \"[f]use|[F]ILESYSTEM_NAME\"\n123: \n124: # 5. 基本连通性测试\n125: ls -la <FUSE_mount_point>\n126: stat <FUSE_mount_point>/test_file 2>&1\n127: ```\n128: \n129: **L1 结论判定**：\n130: \n131: | 现象 | 可能原因 | 下一层 |\n132: |------|---------|--------|\n133: | 挂载点 ls 返回 EIO | FUSE daemon 崩溃 | Branch A |\n134: | ls 卡死/D 状态 | 请求队列阻塞 | Branch B |\n135: | 性能异常慢 | max_read/max_write 配置不当 | Branch C |\n136: | 数据不一致 | writeback cache 问题 | Branch D |\n137: | daemon 进程存在但无响应 | 多线程死锁 | Branch E |\n138: | 权限 denied | /dev/fuse 权限 | Branch F |\n139: | 内核 Panic/Oops | FUSE 内核模块 Bug | Branch G |\n140: | 多种现象共存 | 混合故障 | Branch H |\n141: \n142: ### L2 → L3: 类型层与代码根因层\n143: \n144: #### Branch A — FUSE Daemon 崩溃后 EIO\n145: \n146: **触发条件**：L1 中访问 FUSE 挂载点返回 \"Transport endpoint is not connected\" 或 EIO。\n147: \n148: ```\n149: L2 诊断：\n150: ├── 1. stat <mount_point>（确认 EIO 错误码）\n151: ├── 2. grep <mount_point> /proc/mounts（挂载条目是否仍存在）\n152: ├── 3. ls /sys/fs/fuse/connections/（连接是否已销毁）\n153: ├── 4. ps aux | grep <daemon_name>（daemon 进程是否存在）\n154: ├── 5. journalctl -u <daemon_service> --since \"5 min ago\"（daemon 退出日志）\n155: ├── 6. dmesg | grep -i fuse（内核 FUSE 消息）\n156: ├── 7. cat /sys/fs/fuse/connections/*/abort 2>/dev/null（abort 状态）\n157: │\n158: └── L3 根因判定：\n159:     ├── daemon 进程不存在 + 连接已销毁 → daemon 崩溃/被 OOM Kill\n160:     ├── daemon 进程不存在 + 连接残留 → daemon 退出但连接未清理\n161:     ├── daemon 存在但连接状态异常 → daemon 内部状态机错误\n162:     ├── dmesg 显示 \"fuse: aborting connection\" → 内核主动中止\n163:     ├── OOM Killer 日志 → daemon 因内存超限被内核杀死\n164:     └── 连接 abort 状态为 1 → 手动触发 abort 或 daemon 调用 abort\n165: ```\n166: \n167: **典型输出**：\n168: ```\n169: 结论: FUSE daemon 进程不存在（已崩溃），\n170:       /sys/fs/fuse/connections/ 目录为空（连接已销毁）。\n171:       dmesg 无 FUSE 相关错误，但 journalctl 显示 daemon 因\n172:       SIGSEGV (signal 11) 退出。\n173: 根因: FUSE daemon 程序存在内存访问越界 Bug，导致段错误崩溃。\n174: ```\n175: \n176: #### Branch B — FUSE 请求队列阻塞\n177: \n178: **触发条件**：LS 卡死、进程 D 状态（uninterruptible sleep）、`/sys/fs/fuse/connections/*/waiting` 持续增长。\n179: \n180: ```\n181: L2 诊断：\n182: ├── 1. cat /sys/fs/fuse/connections/*/waiting（请求队列深度）\n183: ├── 2. cat /sys/fs/fuse/connections/*/max_background（最大后台请求数）\n184: ├── 3. ps aux | grep D | grep -v grep（D 状态进程列表）\n185: ├── 4. cat /proc/<D_pid>/stack（查看 D 状态内核栈）\n186: ├── 5. strace -e trace=write,read,ioctl -p <daemon_pid>（daemon 系统调用）\n187: ├── 6. cat /sys/fs/fuse/connections/*/congested_threshold_ms（拥塞阈值）\n188: ├── 7. dmesg | grep -i \"fuse.*block\"（阻塞告警）\n189: │\n190: └── L3 根因判定：\n191:     ├── waiting 持续增长 + daemon 未处理请求 → daemon 侧线程阻塞\n192:     ├── daemon 进程 strace 显示 read() 未被唤醒 → 内核/FUSE 调度问题\n193:     ├── D 状态进程内核栈显示 fuse_request_send → 请求队列已满等待\n194:     ├── max_background 设置过小 → 请求队列排队上限低导致积压\n195:     ├── daemon write() 变慢或阻塞 → daemon 后端存储 I/O 瓶颈\n196:     └── congested_threshold 触发 → FUSE 内核主动限流\n197: ```\n198: \n199: **典型输出**：\n200: ```\n201: 结论: /sys/fs/fuse/connections/*/waiting 持续增长（当前值: 512），\n202:       进程 D 状态栈显示 fuse_request_send。\n203:       strace 显示 daemon read() 调用未被及时唤醒。\n204: 根因: FUSE daemon 工作线程池太小或线程卡在后端 I/O 上，\n205:       无法及时消费内核下发的 FUSE 请求。\n206: ```\n207: \n208: #### Branch C — max_read/max_write 配置不当\n209: \n210: **触发条件**：FUSE 文件系统性能显著低于预期，小文件/大文件读写性能异常。\n211: \n212: ```\n213: L2 诊断：\n214: ├── 1. cat /sys/fs/fuse/connections/*/max_read（当前 FUSE 最大读取大小）\n215: ├── 2. cat /sys/module/fuse/parameters/max_read（内核模块参数）\n216: ├── 3. mount | grep <fuse_type>（挂载参数 -o max_read=,max_write=）\n217: ├── 4. dd if=<mount_point>/test of=/dev/null bs=1M count=100（读性能测试）\n218: ├── 5. dd if=/dev/zero of=<mount_point>/test bs=1M count=100（写性能测试）\n219: ├── 6. iostat -x 1 <device>（底层 I/O 延迟）\n220: ├── 7. strace -e pread64,pwrite64 -p <daemon_pid>（系统调用大小对比）\n221: │\n222: └── L3 根因判定：\n223:     ├── max_read=4096（4K）→ 每次读请求仅传输 4K，大文件读性能极差\n224:     ├── max_write=4096（4K）→ 每次写请求仅传输 4K，写性能瓶颈\n225:     ├── max_read 与底层存储块大小不匹配 → 产生大量小 I/O\n226:     ├── 挂载时未指定 max_read= → 使用默认值（通常 1MB，但某些 FUSE 缩减）\n227:     ├── daemon 未实现 readdir 缓存 → 目录遍历性能退化\n228:     └── 内核 max_read 参数被 sysfs 限制 → 无法超过内核模块设置的上限\n229: ```\n230: \n231: **典型输出**：\n232: ```\n233: 结论: max_read=4096（4K），远低于默认 1MB。\n234:       dd 读测试仅 12 MB/s，远低于预期 200+ MB/s。\n235:       strace 确认每次 pread64 仅传输 4096 字节。\n236: 根因: FUSE 挂载时未指定 max_read，daemon 初始化协商值为 4K\n237:       （libfuse 旧版本默认），导致大文件顺序读性能退化。\n238: ```\n239: \n240: #### Branch D — Writeback Cache 一致性问题\n241: \n242: **触发条件**：FUSE 文件系统写入后读取数据不一致、写入顺序错误、重复内容。\n243: \n244: ```\n245: L2 诊断：\n246: ├── 1. mount | grep <fuse_type> | grep -o \"writeback_cache\"（检查是否启用）\n247: ├── 2. cat /sys/module/fuse/parameters/use_writeback_cache（内核参数）\n248: ├── 3. echo \"test\" > <mount_point>/file && cat <mount_point>/file（一致性测试）\n249: ├── 4. strace -e write,pwrite64,fsync -p <daemon_pid>（跟踪写操作时序）\n250: ├── 5. dd if=/dev/urandom of=<mount_point>/test bs=4K count=100（并发写入）\n251: ├── 6. md5sum <mount_point>/test && sleep 1 && md5sum <mount_point>/test（变化检测）\n252: ├── 7. grep -i \"fuse.*invalidate\" /proc/<daemon_pid>/stack（缓存无效化状态）\n253: │\n254: └── L3 根因判定：\n255:     ├── writeback_cache 启用但 daemon 未实现 ->release 回调 → 数据未刷入后端\n256:     ├── 并发写入后的读取返回过期数据 → page cache 未正确无效化\n257:     ├── daemon write() 返回成功但数据未持久化 → 缺少 fsync 语义\n258:     ├── 内核 fuse_conn 中 writeback_cache=1 但后端不支持原子写\n259:     ├── mmap 写入后数据丢失 → FUSE 不支持 shared mmap writeback cache\n260:     └── multi-page writeback 顺序错误 → daemon 未按 LBA 顺序处理请求\n261: ```\n262: \n263: **典型输出**：\n264: ```\n265: 结论: writeback_cache 启用后，写入 100 个 4K 块后的 md5sum\n266:       在不同读取时间点返回不同值。\n267:       daemon 未实现 ->write() 回调的完整 writeback 语义。\n268: 根因: FUSE daemon 启用 writeback_cache 模式但未正确处理\n269:       内核的 writeback 请求，page cache 与后端存储数据不一致。\n270: ```\n271: \n272: #### Branch E — 多线程 FUSE Daemon 死锁\n273: \n274: **触发条件**：FUSE daemon 进程存在但操作挂起，挂载点操作无响应。\n275: \n276: ```\n277: L2 诊断：\n278: ├── 1. ps -eLf | grep <daemon_name>（daemon 线程列表）\n279: ├── 2. cat /proc/<daemon_pid>/stack（主线程内核栈）\n280: ├── 3. for tid in $(ls /proc/<daemon_pid>/task/); do echo \"TID:$tid\"; cat /proc/$tid/stack 2>/dev/null; done\n281: ├── 4. strace -f -e trace=write,read,ioctl -p <daemon_pid>（多线程追踪）\n282: ├── 5. gdb -p <daemon_pid> -batch -ex \"thread apply all bt\"（全线程回溯）\n283: ├── 6. cat /sys/fs/fuse/connections/*/waiting（确认请求堆积）\n284: ├── 7. kill -USR1 <daemon_pid>（向 daemon 发送信号检查状态）\n285: │\n286: └── L3 根因判定：\n287:     ├── 所有工作线程在 pthread_mutex_lock 等待 → 互斥锁死锁\n288:     ├── 线程 A 持有锁 L1 等待锁 L2，线程 B 持有锁 L2 等待锁 L1 → 经典死锁\n289:     ├── 工作线程在 write() 后端存储时阻塞 → I/O 死锁（等待自身填充）\n290:     ├── 线程池所有线程都在 fuse_session_process 中 → 请求循环依赖\n291:     ├── 主线程在 fuse_loop 中阻塞但工作线程已退出 → 线程管理 Bug\n292:     └── daemon 中 fuse_reply_* 调用顺序错误 → 协议级死锁\n293: ```\n294: \n295: **典型输出**：\n296: ```\n297: 结论: daemon 4 个工作线程全部在 pthread_mutex_lock 等待。\n298:       gdb 显示 Thread 1 持有 lock A 等待 lock B，\n299:       Thread 2 持有 lock B 等待 lock A——经典 ABBA 死锁。\n300: 根因: FUSE daemon 中锁获取顺序不一致，导致多线程死锁，\n301:       文件系统操作完全挂起。\n302: ```\n303: \n304: #### Branch F — /dev/fuse 设备权限问题\n305: \n306: **触发条件**：容器或非 root 用户启动 FUSE daemon 时出现 Permission denied。\n307: \n308: ```\n309: L2 诊断：\n310: ├── 1. ls -la /dev/fuse（设备节点权限）\n311: ├── 2. getfacl /dev/fuse（ACL 权限检查）\n312: ├── 3. cat /proc/<daemon_pid>/status | grep Cap（daemon 能力集）\n313: ├── 4. grep fuse /etc/group（fuse 用户组）\n314: ├── 5. groups <daemon_user>（用户所属组）\n315: ├── 6. cat /etc/fuse.conf（FUSE 全局配置）\n316: ├── 7. capsh --print | grep fuse（进程能力检查）\n317: ├── 8. container environment: cat /proc/1/cgroup（容器内 cgroup 检查）\n318: │\n319: └── L3 根因判定：\n320:     ├── /dev/fuse 权限 0600 root:root → 非 root 用户无法访问\n321:     ├── daemon 用户不在 fuse 组 → 缺少 /dev/fuse 访问权限\n322:     ├── 容器内未挂载 /dev/fuse → 设备节点不存在\n323:     ├── 容器缺少 CAP_SYS_ADMIN 或 CAP_MKNOD → 无法操作 FUSE 设备\n324:     ├── user_allow_other 未在 /etc/fuse.conf 启用 → 无法使用 allow_other\n325:     ├── AppArmor/SELinux 阻止 FUSE 操作 → 安全策略限制\n326:     └── daemon 进程 capabilities 被移除 → container runtime 降权\n327: ```\n328: \n329: **典型输出**：\n330: ```\n331: 结论: /dev/fuse 权限 0600 root:root，daemon 以非 root 用户\n332:       运行且不在 fuse 用户组中。\n333:       daemon 启动日志显示 \"Permission denied\" 打开 /dev/fuse。\n334: 根因: /dev/fuse 设备节点仅 root 可读写，FUSE daemon\n335:       以普通用户运行且未加入 fuse 组，无法打开设备。\n336: ```\n337: \n338: #### Branch G — FUSE 内核模块 Bug\n339: \n340: **触发条件**：内核 Panic、Oops、soft lockup 与 FUSE 相关，或已知 FUSE 内核 Bug。\n341: \n342: ```\n343: L2 诊断：\n344: ├── 1. dmesg | grep -iE \"fuse|libfuse\"（内核 FUSE 消息）\n345: ├── 2. dmesg | grep -iE \"kernel panic|Oops|BUG|soft lockup\"（内核异常）\n346: ├── 3. cat /sys/module/fuse/version（FUSE 模块版本）\n347: ├── 4. uname -r（内核版本）\n348: ├── 5. cat /proc/self/mounts | grep fuse（所有 FUSE 挂载）\n349: ├── 6. cat /sys/fs/fuse/connections/*/abort（abort 状态）\n350: ├── 7. test -f /var/crash/vmcore* 2>/dev/null && ls -lh /var/crash/（crash dump 检查）\n351: ├── 8. grep -i fuse /var/log/messages | tail -20（系统日志）\n352: │\n353: └── L3 根因判定：\n354:     ├── 已知 FUSE 内核 Bug 列表匹配（CVE-xxxx-xxxx / 内核 commit）\n355:     ├── 特定内核版本 + FUSE 版本组合已知不兼容\n356:     ├── CR2 地址在 FUSE 模块区域内 → FUSE 内核模块导致 Panic\n357:     ├── soft lockup 栈显示在 fuse_* 函数中 → FUSE 内核路径问题\n358:     ├── 大规模并发操作触发的竞态条件 → 内核 FUSE 并发 Bug\n359:     └── FUSE 模块参数不合理导致内核异常 → max_read 过小/过大\n360: ```\n361: \n362: **典型输出**：\n363: ```\n364: 结论: dmesg 显示 \"kernel BUG at fs/fuse/dev.c:1234\"，\n365:       内核版本 5.15.0-rc3 存在已知 FUSE 并发访问 Bug。\n366:       CR2 地址 0xffff888123456789 在 fuse_dev_do_write 函数范围内。\n367: 根因: 内核 FUSE 模块在特定内核版本下存在并发竞态条件，\n368:       多线程并发写操作触发内核 BUG。\n369: ```\n370: \n371: #### Branch H — 混合/复杂 FUSE 故障\n372: \n373: **触发条件**：多种现象共存，或以上分支无法覆盖的复杂 FUSE 问题。\n374: \n375: ```\n376: L2 诊断：\n377: ├── 1. 执行所有以上分支的 L2 诊断（汇总所有证据）\n378: ├── 2. 交叉对比各分支症状（判定主次故障）\n379: ├── 3. 完整 strace -f -e trace=all -p <daemon_pid> -o /tmp/strace.log\n380: ├── 4. lsof -p <daemon_pid>（daemon 打开的文件/连接）\n381: ├── 5. tcpdump -i any host <backend_storage_ip>（后端存储网络抓包）\n382: ├── 6. strace -e trace=all ls -la <mount_point> 2>&1（客户端操作全追踪）\n383: ├── 7. 对比故障前后的 FUSE 配置快照（连接数、参数、daemon 版本）\n384: │\n385: └── L3 根因判定：\n386:     ├── 按故障链优先级排序（先解决依赖的下层问题）\n387:     ├── 多故障串联（daemon 崩溃 → 残留连接 → 新 daemon 无法挂载）\n388:     ├── 配置错误叠加（max_read 过小 + 线程池太小 + writeback 未启用）\n389:     ├── 环境变化触发（内核升级、cgroup 限制、SELinux 策略变更）\n390:     └── 复杂的 libfuse API 使用错误（回调注册、会话管理、信号处理）\n391: ```\n392: \n393: **典型输出**：\n394: ```\n395: 结论: 多种故障共存：daemon 线程池过小（4 线程）导致写性能差，\n396:       同时 max_read=4K 进一步退化读性能，writeback cache 启用\n397:       但 daemon 未正确处理 ->write 回调。\n398: 根因: 多重配置叠加导致 FUSE 极端性能退化，建议逐一修复：\n399:       1. 增大线程池至 16+\n400:       2. 设置 max_read=128K+\n401:       3. 检查 writeback cache 回调实现\n402: ```\n403: \n404: ---\n405: \n406: ## 第四节：故障模式速查表\n407: \n408: | 故障模式 | 核心命令 | 特征日志/现象 |\n409: |---------|---------|-------------|\n410: | Daemon 崩溃 EIO | `stat <mount_point>` | `Transport endpoint is not connected` |\n411: | 请求队列阻塞 | `cat .../connections/*/waiting` | `waiting > 0` 且持续增长 |\n412: | max_read/write 不当 | `cat .../connections/*/max_read` | `max_read=4096` 性能异常低 |\n413: | writeback 不一致 | `mount \\| grep writeback_cache` | 写入后读取数据不同 |\n414: | 多线程死锁 | `cat /proc/<pid>/task/*/stack` | `pthread_mutex_lock` 全部阻塞 |\n415: | /dev/fuse 权限 | `ls -la /dev/fuse` | `Permission denied` |\n416: | 内核 Bug | `dmesg \\| grep -i fuse` | `kernel BUG at fs/fuse/dev.c` |\n417: | 混合故障 | 汇总所有诊断 | 多种现象并存 |\n418: \n419: ## 第五节：参考文档\n420: \n421: - `references/fuse_commands.md` — FUSE 诊断命令速查\n422: - `references/fuse_params.md` — 内核 FUSE 相关参数说明\n423: - `references/fuse_patterns.md` — FUSE 故障模式与正则匹配"}
{"step_index":650,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T11:06:47Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-26T11:06:47Z\nCompleted At: 2026-10-26T11:06:48Z\nShowing lines 1-75 of 75\n1: ---\n2: name: fuse\n3: description: Build, debug, and review Linux FUSE filesystems with the official libfuse userspace library. Use when implementing a FUSE filesystem, choosing between libfuse high-level vs low-level APIs, wiring callbacks, building with fuse3/pkg-config, mounting for local testing, or troubleshooting fusermount3 and permission issues.\n4: ---\n5: \n6: # FUSE\n7: \n8: Use the official `libfuse/libfuse` project as the baseline for Linux FUSE work.\n9: \n10: ## Quick Start\n11: \n12: 1. Confirm the task is Linux FUSE userspace work, not kernel module work.\n13: 2. Prefer the official `libfuse` interfaces and examples before suggesting wrappers.\n14: 3. Decide API style:\n15: - Use the high-level API for simpler path-based filesystems.\n16: - Use the low-level API for inode-level control, explicit replies, or advanced behavior.\n17: 4. Build with `pkg-config fuse3 --cflags --libs` unless the project already uses another build system.\n18: 5. For local runs, prefer foreground debug mode first: `-f -d`.\n19: \n20: ## Workflow\n21: \n22: ### 1. Choose the API\n23: \n24: Use the high-level API when the user needs a straightforward filesystem and path callbacks are sufficient.\n25: Read `include/fuse.h` semantics first.\n26: \n27: Use the low-level API when the user needs inode handling, async-style explicit replies, or finer control over request lifetime.\n28: Read `include/fuse_lowlevel.h` semantics first.\n29: \n30: ### 2. Start from official examples\n31: \n32: Check the `example/` directory in `libfuse/libfuse` before drafting handlers from scratch.\n33: For passthrough, mirror, hello-world, or minimal callback wiring, adapt an official example instead of inventing a new skeleton.\n34: \n35: ### 3. Build correctly\n36: \n37: Use these defaults unless the project already defines them:\n38: \n39: ```bash\n40: pkg-config fuse3 --cflags --libs\n41: ```\n42: \n43: Typical manual build pattern:\n44: \n45: ```bash\n46: gcc fs.c -o fs $(pkg-config fuse3 --cflags --libs)\n47: ```\n48: \n49: If the project vendors `libfuse`, follow its existing Meson/Ninja setup instead of replacing the build flow.\n50: \n51: ### 4. Run and debug safely\n52: \n53: Use a writable, non-sticky mountpoint owned by the current user.\n54: Start in foreground debug mode first:\n55: \n56: ```bash\n57: ./fs -f -d <mountpoint>\n58: ```\n59: \n60: If mounting fails, check:\n61: - `fusermount3` availability\n62: - `/etc/fuse.conf`\n63: - `allow_other` vs `default_permissions`\n64: - whether the mountpoint is writable by the mounting user\n65: \n66: ### 5. Troubleshoot by symptom\n67: \n68: If callbacks are not firing, verify the mount succeeded and the process is still in foreground.\n69: If permission behavior is surprising, inspect `default_permissions` and `allow_other`.\n70: If the filesystem hangs, inspect whether a low-level handler failed to send a reply.\n71: If performance is poor, check whether the design needs low-level API control, cache tuning, or fewer round trips.\n72: \n73: ## Read Next\n74: \n75: Read `references/official-libfuse.md` when you need the official repo, docs, build flow, and the canonical places to look for examples and headers."}
{"step_index":651,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T11:06:48Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-26T11:06:48Z\nCompleted At: 2026-10-26T11:06:48Z\nShowing lines 1-352 of 352\n1: ---\n2: name: rust-memory-optimization\n3: description: |\n4:   Memory optimization and allocation reduction in Rust. Use when:\n5:   - User is designing memory-sensitive or low-latency systems\n6:   - Optimizing data structures to reduce memory footprint\n7:   - Replacing heap allocations with stack-allocated/bounded structures (SmallVec, ArrayVec, ThinVec)\n8:   - Handling small strings with optimizations (CompactString)\n9:   - Reusing collections via clear() in loops\n10:   - Implementing zero-copy decoding and references\n11:   - Structuring arena-allocated memory (Bumpalo)\n12:   - Measuring memory usage, profiling heap, or diagnosing leaks\n13: ---\n14: \n15: \n16: \n17: ## Quick Navigation\n18: \n19: - [references/stack_allocations.md](references/stack_allocations.md)\n20: - [references/arenas.md](references/arenas.md)\n21: \n22: # Rust Memory Optimization Guide\n23: \n24: Advanced strategies for reducing allocations, shrinking layout sizes, and boosting performance.\n25: \n26: ## Core Rules & Patterns\n27: \n28: ### 1. Bounded Heap-Free Collections\n29: For collections that are usually small, avoid standard vectors to bypass heap allocations.\n30: - **`SmallVec`**: Stack-allocated up to a threshold, overflows to the heap.\n31: - **`ArrayVec`**: Fixed-capacity array wrapper; never allocates on the heap.\n32: - **`ThinVec`**: Only takes a single pointer size when empty, reducing size in enum layouts.\n33: \n34: ```rust\n35: use smallvec::{smallvec, SmallVec};\n36: use arrayvec::ArrayVec;\n37: \n38: // SmallVec: Allocates 4 items on the stack. Goes to heap only if count > 4.\n39: let mut local_tags: SmallVec<[String; 4]> = smallvec![];\n40: local_tags.push(\"Rust\".to_string());\n41: \n42: // ArrayVec: Absolute limit of 8 items on the stack. No heap overflow.\n43: let mut coordinates: ArrayVec<f64, 8> = ArrayVec::new();\n44: coordinates.push(42.0);\n45: ```\n46: \n47: ### 2. Small String Optimization (SSO)\n48: Standard `String` consumes 24 bytes and allocates heap space immediately. Use `CompactString` for inline small strings (under 24 bytes) without allocating.\n49: \n50: ```rust\n51: use compact_str::CompactString;\n52: \n53: // No heap allocation for strings <= 24 characters\n54: let username = CompactString::new(\"user_123\");\n55: ```\n56: \n57: ### 3. Boxed Slices vs Vectors\n58: If a collection's size is determined once at initialization and never changes, convert it from `Vec<T>` to `Box<[T]>` to save 8 bytes of stack capacity space.\n59: \n60: ```rust\n61: let items_vec: Vec<i32> = vec![1, 2, 3];\n62: \n63: // Save capacity field (shrinks stack representation from 24 to 16 bytes)\n64: let items_slice: Box<[i32]> = items_vec.into_boxed_slice();\n65: ```\n66: \n67: ### 4. Zero-Copy Patterns\n68: Instead of cloning or allocating strings, hold references to existing memory using slices or crates like `bytes::Bytes`.\n69: \n70: ```rust\n71: use bytes::Bytes;\n72: \n73: pub struct Message {\n74:     // Zero-copy reference-counted byte buffer slice\n75:     pub payload: Bytes,\n76: }\n77: \n78: // Can be sliced and shared among threads without cloning underlying memory\n79: let original = Bytes::from(vec![0; 1024]);\n80: let slice = original.slice(0..100); \n81: ```\n82: \n83: ### 5. Arena Allocation\n84: For batch allocation where structures share a lifecycle (e.g. AST parsing), use arena allocators (`bumpalo`) to allocate items sequentially in a continuous region of memory and free them all at once.\n85: \n86: ```rust\n87: use bumpalo::Bump;\n88: \n89: let bump = Bump::new();\n90: \n91: // Allocates quickly on the bump arena\n92: let string_ref = bump.alloc_str(\"dynamic string\");\n93: let int_ref = bump.alloc(42);\n94: \n95: // Entire arena is cleared at once on drop\n96: ```\n97: \n98: ### 6. Collection Reuse\n99: Reuse collection allocations in performance-critical loops with `.clear()` instead of re-instantiating.\n100: \n101: ```rust\n102: // Bad: Allocates a new vector every iteration\n103: for item in feed {\n104:     let mut batch = Vec::new();\n105:     batch.push(item);\n106: }\n107: \n108: // Good: Reuses allocation buffer\n109: let mut batch = Vec::with_capacity(100);\n110: for item in feed {\n111:     batch.clear();\n112:     batch.push(item);\n113: }\n114: ```\n115: \n116: ## Layout Awareness\n117: \n118: Use `std::mem::size_of` to understand data layout.\n119: \n120: ```rust\n121: println!(\"User size: {}\", std::mem::size_of::<User>());\n122: ```\n123: \n124: Reorder fields to reduce padding only when the type is numerous or hot.\n125: \n126: ```rust\n127: // Often smaller: group large-alignment fields first\n128: struct Record {\n129:     id: u64,\n130:     flags: u32,\n131:     kind: u8,\n132: }\n133: ```\n134: \n135: ## String Strategy\n136: \n137: ```rust\n138: fn label<'a>(name: &'a str, fallback: &'a str) -> std::borrow::Cow<'a, str> {\n139:     if name.is_empty() { fallback.into() } else { name.into() }\n140: }\n141: ```\n142: \n143: Avoid `format!` in tight loops. Reuse buffers with `clear()`.\n144: \n145: ## Zero-Copy Parsing\n146: \n147: Return slices into the input when the input outlives parsed data.\n148: \n149: ```rust\n150: pub struct Header<'a> {\n151:     pub name: &'a str,\n152:     pub value: &'a str,\n153: }\n154: ```\n155: \n156: Do not force zero-copy when it creates unmanageable lifetimes for little gain.\n157: \n158: ## ThinVec for Enum Payloads\n159: \n160: When enums contain `Vec` variants, `ThinVec` reduces the enum size by storing only a pointer when empty:\n161: \n162: ```rust\n163: use thin_vec::ThinVec;\n164: \n165: // Regular Vec in an enum makes the enum 24+ bytes even when empty\n166: enum Node {\n167:     Leaf(i64),\n168:     Children(Vec<Node>),     // 24 bytes for Vec\n169: }\n170: \n171: // ThinVec only stores 8 bytes (a pointer) when empty\n172: enum NodeOptimized {\n173:     Leaf(i64),\n174:     Children(ThinVec<Node>), // 8 bytes for ThinVec\n175: }\n176: ```\n177: \n178: ## Cow for Conditional Ownership\n179: \n180: ```rust\n181: use std::borrow::Cow;\n182: \n183: pub struct Error {\n184:     message: Cow<'static, str>,\n185: }\n186: \n187: impl Error {\n188:     // No allocation for static messages\n189:     pub fn new(msg: &'static str) -> Self {\n190:         Self { message: Cow::Borrowed(msg) }\n191:     }\n192: \n193:     // Allocates only when dynamic\n194:     pub fn with_detail(msg: String) -> Self {\n195:         Self { message: Cow::Owned(msg) }\n196:     }\n197: }\n198: ```\n199: \n200: ## Arc vs Rc Trade-offs\n201: \n202: ```rust\n203: use std::rc::Rc;\n204: use std::sync::Arc;\n205: \n206: // Single-threaded shared ownership — cheaper than Arc\n207: let shared = Rc::new(large_data);\n208: \n209: // Multi-threaded shared ownership — required across threads\n210: let shared = Arc::new(large_data);\n211: ```\n212: \n213: Prefer `Rc` when data never crosses thread boundaries. `Arc` adds atomic reference counting overhead.\n214: \n215: ## HashMap Memory Optimization\n216: \n217: ```rust\n218: use hashbrown::HashMap;\n219: \n220: // hashbrown's HashMap uses less memory than std's and is faster\n221: let mut map: HashMap<String, i32> = HashMap::with_capacity(128);\n222: \n223: // Reserve capacity upfront to avoid rehashing\n224: map.reserve(expected_count);\n225: \n226: // Consider FxHashMap for non-adversarial keys\n227: use rustc_hash::FxHashMap;\n228: let mut fast_map: FxHashMap<String, i32> = FxHashMap::default();\n229: ```\n230: \n231: ## Stack vs Heap Decision Matrix\n232: \n233: | Type | Stack Size | Heap Alloc | Use When |\n234: |------|-----------|------------|----------|\n235: | `String` | 24 bytes | Yes | Owns mutable text |\n236: | `&str` | 16 bytes | No | Borrowed text, lifetime bound |\n237: | `CompactString` | 24 bytes | No (≤24 chars) | Short strings that own data |\n238: | `Cow<str>` | 32 bytes | Conditionally | Mostly static, rarely dynamic |\n239: | `Box<str>` | 16 bytes | Yes | Owned fixed string |\n240: | `Vec<T>` | 24 bytes | Yes | Growable collection |\n241: | `SmallVec<[T; N]>` | ~24+ bytes | Only if >N | Usually small, occasionally large |\n242: | `Box<[T]>` | 16 bytes | Yes | Fixed-size after construction |\n243: | `ThinVec<T>` | 8 bytes | Only if non-empty | Empty or small in enums |\n244: \n245: ## Measuring Memory\n246: \n247: ```rust\n248: use std::alloc::{GlobalAlloc, System, Layout};\n249: \n250: struct TrackingAllocator;\n251: \n252: unsafe impl GlobalAlloc for TrackingAllocator {\n253:     unsafe fn alloc(&self, layout: Layout) -> *mut u8 {\n254:         System.alloc(layout)\n255:     }\n256: \n257:     unsafe fn dealloc(&self, ptr: *mut u8, layout: Layout) {\n258:         System.dealloc(ptr, layout)\n259:     }\n260: }\n261: \n262: // For detailed profiling, use dhat, heaptrack, or valgrind\n263: ```\n264: \n265: Use `dhat` crate for heap profiling in tests:\n266: \n267: ```rust\n268: #[cfg(test)]\n269: mod tests {\n270:     #[test]\n271:     fn memory_test() {\n272:         let _profiler = dhat::Profiler::new_heap();\n273:         // code under test\n274:         // dhat prints allocation stats on drop\n275:     }\n276: }\n277: ```\n278: \n279: ## Optimization Workflow\n280: \n281: 1. Measure allocations and CPU first.\n282: 2. Identify the hot path and expected data sizes.\n283: 3. Pick the narrowest memory change.\n284: 4. Benchmark before/after.\n285: 5. Keep readability unless the win is meaningful.\n286: \n287: ## Allocation Decision Rules\n288: \n289: - `Vec<T>`: general purpose growable collection.\n290: - `SmallVec<[T; N]>`: usually-small collection with occasional heap spill.\n291: - `ArrayVec<T, N>`: hard maximum size, no heap allocation.\n292: - `Box<[T]>`: fixed-size heap slice after construction.\n293: - `Bytes`: shared immutable byte buffers.\n294: - `Bump`: many same-lifetime allocations.\n295: - `Cow<'a, T>`: borrow unless mutation/ownership is required.\n296: \n297: ## Anti-Patterns\n298: \n299: ```rust\n300: // Bad: cloning a large Vec just to avoid lifetime complexity\n301: let data = original.clone(); // expensive and unnecessary\n302: \n303: // Good: use Arc or Cow for shared ownership\n304: let data: Arc<[u8]> = original.into();\n305: ```\n306: \n307: ```rust\n308: // Bad: allocating inside a hot loop\n309: for item in items {\n310:     let s = format!(\"processing {}\", item); // allocates every iteration\n311: }\n312: \n313: // Good: reuse a buffer\n314: let mut buf = String::with_capacity(128);\n315: for item in items {\n316:     buf.clear();\n317:     write!(buf, \"processing {}\", item).unwrap();\n318: }\n319: ```\n320: \n321: - Replacing every `Vec` with `SmallVec` without measuring.\n322: - Keeping arena references after reset.\n323: - Cloning strings to satisfy ownership instead of shortening borrow scopes.\n324: - Using `Arc` as a default clone workaround.\n325: - Optimizing layout for types created a handful of times.\n326: - Using `Box<dyn Trait>` when generics would eliminate the allocation entirely.\n327: \n328: ## Review Prompt\n329: \n330: When reviewing memory optimization, ask what was measured, which allocation is removed, what lifetime assumptions changed, and whether the new type increases stack size or API complexity.\n331: \n332: ## Optimization Checklist\n333: \n334: - Measure allocations before changing data structures.\n335: - Preallocate collections only when capacity is known or bounded.\n336: - Prefer borrowing and `Cow` before cloning strings or buffers.\n337: - Use arenas only when lifetimes are truly batch-scoped.\n338: - Check stack growth when replacing heap allocations with inline storage.\n339: - Re-benchmark after changes and keep the simpler version if gains are noise.\n340: - Profile with `dhat` or `heaptrack` to find actual allocation hotspots.\n341: - Consider `hashbrown` or `rustc-hash` for HashMap-heavy code.\n342: \n343: ## References\n344: \n345: - [Rust Performance Book: Heap Allocations](https://nnethercote.github.io/perf-book/heap-allocations.html)\n346: - [smallvec](https://docs.rs/smallvec)\n347: - [arrayvec](https://docs.rs/arrayvec)\n348: - [bumpalo](https://docs.rs/bumpalo)\n349: - [compact_str](https://docs.rs/compact_str)\n350: - [bytes](https://docs.rs/bytes)\n351: - [dhat](https://docs.rs/dhat)\n352: - [hashbrown](https://docs.rs/hashbrown)"}
